#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kate;"
msgstr "Apontiaedje di &kate;"

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: configuring.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "configure"
msgstr "apontyî"

#. Tag: secondary
#: configuring.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "settings"
msgstr "apontiaedjes"

#. Tag: tertiary
#: configuring.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "preferences"
msgstr "preferinces"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; offers several means of tweaking the application to behave as "
"desired. The most important ones are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Configuration Dialog"
msgstr "Li purnea d'pontiaedje"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main configuration tool, allowing you to configure the &kate; "
"application, the editor component and the usage of plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr "Li menu <guimenu>Apontiaedjes</guimenu>"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to change often used settings, and to launch the configuration "
"dialogs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>View</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr "Li menu <guimenu>Vey</guimenu>"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to split the current frame, as well as to display the icons and "
"line numbers pane for the currently edited document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The embedded &konsole; is using the configuration defined in the "
"&kcontrolcenter;, and may be configured by clicking the "
"<mousebutton>right</mousebutton> mouse button and choosing from the "
"<guimenuitem>Settings</guimenuitem> sub menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Configuration Dialog"
msgstr "Li purnea des mwaissès apontiaedjes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kate; configuration dialog displays a tree of topics on the left, and a "
"configuration page corresponding to the selected topic on the right. The "
"tree groups the pages of the dialog into logical groups."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kate; group"
msgstr "Li groupe &kate;"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "This group contains pages to configure the main &kate; application"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "The General Page"
msgstr "Li pådje djeneråle"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Global Options for &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Application Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: configuring.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>MDI</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>MDI</primary>"

#. Tag: secondary
#: configuring.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>SDI</secondary>"
msgstr "<secondary>SDI</secondary>"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group lets you choose between &kate; <acronym>MDI</acronym> and &kate; "
"<acronym>SDI</acronym> mode, selecting the appropriate button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; <acronym>MDI</acronym> (Multiple Document Interface), which is the "
"default mode, makes &kate; use a single window for all open files. You can "
"choose the document to edit from the File List (docked into the &kate; "
"window by default) or by selecting the document from the "
"<guimenu>Document</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; <acronym>SDI</acronym> (Single Document Interface) will make &kate; "
"open each document in a window of its own, and the File List/File Selector "
"will have a separate window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you change this setting, you will need to restart &kate; for it to take "
"effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "At Startup"
msgstr "A l' enondaedje"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These options determine how and if &kate; will restore your editing session "
"when launched after a normal shutdown (if restored by the session manager, "
"&kate; will always attempt to restore your session as close as possible to "
"what it was when you last used &kate;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reopen Files"
msgstr "Ridrovi les fitchîs"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, files open when you last closed &kate; will be "
"reopened. Bookmarks will be restored, and the cursor position, icon border "
"and line numbers settings for the last editor used with the document will be "
"reestablished"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restore View Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, &kate; will attempt to restore your frames "
"exactly as you left them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restrict to single instance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enabling this means you can only have one running instance of &kate; running "
"at any given time. If you attempt to start another one, the current instance "
"will take over and also open files as requested. For example, if you use "
"&kate; for displaying sources for web pages in Konqueror, they will all be "
"opened in an existing instance of &kate; if this option is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Contents While Resizing Frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, the windows will be fully repainted while "
"dragging the frame splitters. If unchecked, a so-called <quote>rubber "
"band</quote> (indicating the new size of the frame) will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sync Konsole with Active Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will cause the built-in &konsole; to <command>cd</command> into the "
"directory of the active document when launched and when a new document gets "
"the focus. If not enabled, you have to do all your navigation in the "
"&konsole; on your own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of Recent Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unsurprisingly, this allows you to decide how long the <guimenu>Open "
"Recent</guimenu> files menu should grow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:164
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "The Doucment List Page"
msgstr "Li pådje des fontes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to enable or disable the background shading "
"visualization of your recent activity, and chose which colors to use if "
"enabled. See the section about <link "
"linkend=\"kate-mdi-tools-file-list\">The Document List</link>"
" for more about this feature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "External Tools"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> menu you will find a submenu labeled "
"<guisubmenu>External Tools</guisubmenu>. These tools invokes external "
"applications with data related to the current document, for example its URL, "
"directory, text or selection. This page allows you to manage the menu and "
"edit, remove or add new tools."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each external tool is a shell command which contains macros representing the "
"document data. When activated, the macros are substituted with data from the "
"active document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "External Tools Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "Label"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "A friendly label for the External Tools menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "Script"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The script to execute when the tool is activated. Before passing the script "
"to the shell, the following macros are substituted:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "%URL"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The full URL of the current document, or an empty string if the document is "
"unsaved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "%URLS"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A space seperated list of the URLs of all open documents (except unsaved "
"ones)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "%directory"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The directory part of the current documents URL or an empty string if the "
"current document is unsaved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "%filename"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the filename of the current document without the path, or an empty string if "
"the current document is unsaved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "%line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "The line number of the insertion cursor is in the current document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "%column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "The column number of the insertion cursor in the current document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "%selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The selected text in the current document, or an empty string if no text is "
"selected"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:241
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "%text"
msgstr "Contecse"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The full text of the current document. Beware that this will potentially "
"exceed the maximum command length allowed on your system. Use with care."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Executable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main executable i the script. This is mandatory, and is used to test if "
"the command can be run at all. A fully qualified path is allowed in case the "
"executable is not in your <envar>PATH</envar> variable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:260 configuring.docbook:706
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mimetypes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A semicolon separated list of mimetypes for which this command should be "
"enabled. This is currently unused."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "Save"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can optionally select to have the current or all documents saved prior "
"to executing the script. This is handy if your script reads the file from "
"disk."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Line Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you fill this, the tool will be available in the <link "
"linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-commandline\">editors command line</link> "
"as <command>exttool-<replaceable>Command Line Name</replaceable></command> "
"(the string you enter here prepended <quote>exttool-</quote>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Editor Group"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group contains all pages related to the editor component of &kate;. "
"Most of the settings here are defaults, they can be overridden by <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-filetypes\">defining a filetype</link>, by "
"<link linkend=\"config-variables\">Document Variables</link> or by changing "
"them pr. document during an editing session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Colors</guilabel> Page"
msgstr "Li pådje des <guilabel>Coleurs</guilabel>"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to change the background and selection background "
"colors of the editor. Initially, &kate; will use the colors as set in the "
"&kcontrolcenter; "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Look'n'Feel</guimenu><guimenuitem>Colors</guimenuitem> "
"</menuchoice> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change a color, press the associated button and select the desired color "
"in the color chooser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choosing the background color may render Syntax Highlighted text unreadable. "
"You should use a light color for the background, and a dark color for the "
"selection background."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Otherwise, you will probably need to change the <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-highlight-default-styles\">Default "
"Styles</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Fonts Page"
msgstr "Li pådje des fontes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to choose the default fonts for &kate;. The settings "
"will be used for the &kwrite; and for viewing text files in &konqueror; as "
"well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The page presents two tabs, one for the editor font and one for the printing "
"font. Select a tab and choose the desired font. The default is to use the "
"&kde; global setting for fixed font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As it is not currently possible to use individual fonts for documents, nor "
"to change the font for printing from the print dialog, be careful. A "
"fixed-width font is strongly recommended."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Indent Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "This page allows you to change the behavior of indentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indent Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto indent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, &kate; will automatically indent new lines equal to the previous "
"line. If the previous line is blank, the nearest above line with contents is "
"used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indent with Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "If checked, &kate; will indent with spaces rather than tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backspace key indents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, &kate; will unindent equal to the nearest above line "
"with contents when you press the <keycap>Backspace</keycap> key if the part "
"of the line preceding the cursor contains only whitespace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab key indents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, &kate; will indent the current line equal to the nearest "
"above line with content when you press the <keycap>Tab</keycap> key, if the "
"part of the line preceding the cursor contains only whitespace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep extra spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this behavior checked, &kate; will leave whitespace behind the cursor "
"after indenting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Select Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid "This page provides options for fine tuning the select behavior of &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid "Persistent Selections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When Persistent Selections is enabled, key input will not cause the "
"selection to be removed/diminished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option partly conflicts with the Overwrite Selection option. If both "
"are enabled, pasting text or pressing any other keys than the arrow keys "
"will cause the selection to be overwritten."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overwrite Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is enabled, any text insertion, whether typed or pasted will cause "
"the selected text to be deleted and replaced with the inserted text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Edit Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page contains miscellaneous options for fine-tuning the behavior of the "
"&kate; editor component."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editor Options"
msgstr "Tchuzes di l' aspougneu"

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid "Word Wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Word Wrap as used here means dynamically format the text by breaking lines "
"at an appropriate place, rather than soft wrapping lines in the editor for "
"easier reading."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will insert a line break as defined by the <link "
"linkend=\"document-end-of-line\">End of Line</link>"
" setting for the document when the line extends the length set in <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-edit-wrap-words-at\">Wrap Words At</link> "
"option described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wrap Words At"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option decides the max length of lines if the <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-edit-word-wrap\">Word Wrap</link> option is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace Tabs with Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will replace inserted <keycap>Tab</keycap> characters "
"with a number of single whitespace characters as defined in <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-edit-tab-indent-width\">Tab Width</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove trailing spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will remove any whitespace at the rear end of a line each "
"time the cursor is moved off that line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab/Indent Width"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:501
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the tab width, which is also used to decide the amount of indentation "
"when <link linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-indent-auto-indent\">Auto "
"Indent</link> is enabled, or indentation is otherwise called for."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the <link linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-indent\">Indent</link>"
" settings indentation may be caused by pressing the <keycap>Tab</keycap>"
" and <keycap>Backspace</keycap> keys, and activating the <link "
"linkend=\"edit-indent\"><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Indent</guimenuitem></link> menu entry will call for indent as "
"well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:514
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto Brackets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is enabled, &kate; will automatically insert a right bracket "
"immediately to the right of the cursor when a left bracket is inserted from "
"the keyboard. The supported bracket types are <keycap>(</keycap>, "
"<keycap>{</keycap>, <keycap>[</keycap>and <keycap>&lt;</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid "Group undos"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will group any number of similar editing actions (for "
"example typing, backspacing, pasting) in one entry in the undo history, so "
"they can all be undone at once."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Tabs"
msgstr "Mostrer les tabulåcions"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:542
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will draw a small dot at the start of a "
"<keycap>Tab</keycap> character in the editor to indicate its presence."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid "Smart Home"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will make &kate; move the cursor to the first non-whitespace character "
"of the current line rather than to the absolute beginning, when the "
"<keycap>Home</keycap> key (or other key assigned to that function) is "
"pressed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wrap Cursor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, moving the cursor past the end of a line will cause it to "
"continue to the next/previous line if any."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not enabled, the cursor cannot be moved right of the beginning of the "
"line, but it may be moved past the end of line, and when text is inserted "
"&kate; will automatically insert whitespace up to that position. This is "
"sometimes very handy for programmers, for example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Keyboard Page"
msgstr "Li pådje del taprece"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:598
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can configure the keyboard shortcuts for the internal commands of "
"the &kate; editor component. These includes commands for moving around in "
"the document and selecting text. For keys related to copying and pasting "
"text, see The Configure Keys Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid "You may change the keys for a command, or add an alternate key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid "To change the key(s) for a command, follow this procedure:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:610
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the command for which you want to configure the keys."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the <guibutton>None</guibutton> option in the pane below the list if "
"you don't want a key for this command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:615
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the <guibutton>Default</guibutton> option to use the default key(s) "
"for the command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the <guibutton>Custom</guibutton> option to select a custom key for "
"the command, or set an alternate one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose the <guibutton>Custom</guibutton> option, the key entering "
"button at the right of the pane will be enabled. To set a key, press it. The "
"&kde; Define Shortcut Dialog will appear. In this dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:629
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose whether to set the default or alternate key. "
"<guilabel>Default</guilabel> does not mean that you change the application "
"default for this action, rather it sets the custom standard key for it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press the desired key sequence, it will be visualized for you in the dialog "
"for your confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are of an adventurous nature, try playing around with the "
"<guibutton>Multikey</guibutton> option. Using it will allow you to have "
"&Emacs;-like key sequences (one key enters a group, the next performs the "
"action), apart from the fact that instead of just doing the job, &kde; will "
"pop up a menu to choose from in an undefined and most likely inappropriate "
"place. You will now be in no doubt as to whether pressing the next key in "
"the sequence will work, or you have to type the menu accelerator (both will "
"work)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:653
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "The Filetypes Page"
msgstr "Li pådje des fontes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allow you to override the default configuration for documents of "
"specified mimetypes. When the editor loads a document, it will try if it "
"matches the file masks or mimetypes for one of the defined filetypes, and if "
"so apply the variables defined. If more filetypes matches, the one with the "
"highest priority will be used. Please see the section <link "
"linkend=\"config-variables\">Configuring With Document Variables</link> for "
"how to specify variables."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a filetype, press the <guibutton>New</guibutton> button and fill "
"in the properties."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove an existing filtype, select it from the dropdown list and press "
"the <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:670
#, no-c-format
msgid "To edit an existing filtype, select it from the dropdown list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:674
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filetype Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:677
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:678
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a friendly name that can be displayed in the "
"<menuchoice><guisubmenu>Tools</guisubmenu><guisubmenu>Filetypes</guisubmenu>"
"</menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:684
#, no-c-format
msgid "Section"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A submenu of "
"<menuchoice><guisubmenu>Tools</guisubmenu><guisubmenu>Filetypes</guisubmenu>"
"</menuchoice> in which to place this filtype. If the section does not "
"allready exist, it will be created for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:692
#, no-c-format
msgid "Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is where the actual configuration goes. Variables set here will "
"overwrite the default configuration values. Please refer to <link "
"linkend=\"config-variables\">Configuring With Document Variables</link> for "
"the available variables."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:700
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Extensions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A semicolon separated list of filename globs used to determine if a document "
"matches this filetype."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A semicolon separated list of mime types, used to determine if a document "
"matches this filetype."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:712
#, no-c-format
msgid "Priority"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:713
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a document matches several filetypes, the one with the highest priority "
"will be chosen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Spelling Page"
msgstr "Li pådje del coridjrece"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:723
#, no-c-format
msgid "This page allows you to configure how &kspell; behaves with &kate;"
msgstr "Cisse pådje ci c' est po-z apontyî li dujhance di &kspell; avou &kate;"

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:727
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Highlighting Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to fine tune the color and syntax type selection of "
"&kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:735
#, no-c-format
msgid "For more in depth information on the syntax highlighting system, see ??"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The page consists of two tabs, one for setting the <guibutton>Default "
"styles</guibutton> and one for managing the <guibutton>Highlight "
"Modes</guibutton>"
". Both tabs display a list of contexts in which the default colors and font "
"are used to visualize the look of each style. The context name is painted "
"using the current properties of the context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:744
#, no-c-format
msgid "The list has four or five columns, each with the following purpose:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:750
#, no-c-format
msgid "Context"
msgstr "Contecse"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays the context name, painted using the style properties for the "
"context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:756
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bold"
msgstr "Cråssès letes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:757
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The state of this checkbox decides if the context should be rendered using a "
"boldface font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:763
#, no-c-format
msgid "Italic"
msgstr "Clintcheyès letes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:764
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The state of this checkbox decides if the context should be rendered using "
"italic font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:769
#, no-c-format
msgid "Normal"
msgstr "Normå"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:770
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button displays the color for drawing the style in normal mode, when "
"the text is not selected that is. To change the color, click the button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:775
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selected"
msgstr "Tchoezi"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:776
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button displays the color for drawing the style when the text is "
"selected. To change the color, click the button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Default"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This checkbox, only available in the <guibutton>Highlight Modes</guibutton> "
"tab shows if the style is using its default values. It will automatically "
"become unchecked if you change any properties of the style. Check it to "
"reset a style to using defaults."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:792
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Default Styles Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:793
#, no-c-format
msgid "To change any of the default styles, set its properties as desired."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:797
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Highlight Modes Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: configuring.docbook:799
#, no-c-format
msgid "syntax highlighting, configuring"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:799
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can change the most important properties of each available "
"highlight mode. First, use the <guibutton>Highlight</guibutton> dropdown to "
"choose a mode to work on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:803
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Highlight modes are initially chosen based on the &MIME; type and extension "
"of the file. To change the list for the current selection, edit the "
"<guibutton>File Extensions</guibutton> and <guibutton>Mime Types</guibutton>"
" entries. Alternatively, press the wizard button to the right of the "
"<guibutton>Mime Types</guibutton> entry. This will show a dialog displaying "
"all available &MIME; types to choose from. Using it will edit the &MIME; "
"types as well as the file extensions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:815
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &MIME; type chooser dialog displays a tree of available &MIME; types, "
"with a description and the patterns for the &MIME; type. To include a &MIME; "
"type, check the box beside it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:821
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can change the style properties of any context as described above."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:824
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the tab, below the highlight properties, you see a button "
"labeled <guibutton>Download</guibutton>"
". Pressing it will attempt to connect to the &kate; website and fetch a list "
"of available syntax highlight modes which you can update or add."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:837
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Plugins Group"
msgstr "Li groupe des tchôke-divins"

#. Tag: primary
#: configuring.docbook:839
#, no-c-format
msgid "plugins, configuring"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:839
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group contains pages related to plugins. Apart from the Manager "
"configuration page, some plugins provide individual configuration options. "
"For information on these, see the documentation for the individual plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:846
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Plugin Manager Page"
msgstr "Li pådje di manaedjmitn des tchôke-divins"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:848
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page provides the means of loading/unloading plugins, and minimal "
"information about individual plugins."
msgstr ""
"Cisse pådje ci c' est po tcherdjî/distcherdjî les tchôke-divins, eyet "
"po des informåcions di båze so tchaeke des tchôke-divins."

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:851
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To load an unloaded plugin, select it in the <guibutton>Available "
"Plugins</guibutton> pane and use the arrow buttons to move it to the "
"<guibutton>Loaded Plugins</guibutton> pane."
msgstr ""
"Po tcherdjî on tchôke-divins ki n' l' est nén co, tchoezixhoz l' e "
"panea des <guibutton>Tchôke-divins k' i gn a</guibutton>"
" eyet eployîz les botons avou les fletches pol displaecî viè l' panea "
"<guibutton>Tchôke-divins tcherdjîs</guibutton>."

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:855
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To unload a loaded plugin, select it in the <guibutton>Loaded "
"Plugins</guibutton> pane and use the arrow buttons to move it to the "
"<guibutton>Available buttons</guibutton> pane."
msgstr ""
"Po distcherdjî on tchôke-divins di tcherdjî, tchoezixhoz l' e panea "
"<guibutton>Tchôke-divins tcherdjîs</guibutton> eyet eployîz les botons "
"avou les fletches pol displaecî viè l' panea des <guibutton>Botons k' i "
"gn a</guibutton>."

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:859
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To view a minimal description and information about a plugin, select it and "
"the information will be available below the lists."
msgstr ""
"Po vey on court discrijhaedje eyet informåcion so on tchôke-divins, "
"tchoezixhoz l' eyet si informåcion serè håynêye pa dzo les djivêyes."

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:870
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring With Document Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:872
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Kate variables is kateparts implementation of document variables, similar to "
"emacs and vi modelines. In katepart, the lines has the format "
"<userinput>kate: VARIABLENAME VALUE; [ VARIABLENAME VALUE; ... ]</userinput>"
" the lines can of cause be in a comment, if the file is in a format with "
"comments. Variable names are single words (no whitespace), and anything up "
"to the next semicolon is the value. The semicolon is required."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:881
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is an example variable line, forcing indentation settings for a C++, "
"java or javascript file:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: configuring.docbook:884
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"// kate: space-indent on; indent-width 4; mixedindent off; indent-mode "
"cstyle;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:887
#, no-c-format
msgid "Only the first and last 10 lines are searched for variable lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:889
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are variables to support almost all configurations in katepart, and "
"aditionally plugins can use variables, in which case it should be documented "
"in the plugin's documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:894
#, no-c-format
msgid "How kate uses variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:896
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When reading configuration, katepart looks in the following places (in that "
"order): <itemizedlist> <listitem><para>The global "
"configuration.</para></listitem> <listitem><para>Optional session "
"data.</para></listitem> <listitem><para>The \"Filetype\" "
"configuration.</para></listitem> <listitem><para>Document variables in the "
"document itself.</para></listitem> <listitem><para>Settings made during "
"editing from menu or command line.</para></listitem> </itemizedlist> As you "
"can understand document variables has the next highest precedence. Whenever "
"a document is saved, the document variables are reread, and will overwrite "
"changes made using menu items or the command line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:911
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any variable not listed below is stored in the document and can be queried "
"by other objects such as plugins, which can use them for their own purpose. "
"For example the variable indent mode uses document variables for its "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:916
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The variables listed here documents &kate; version 2.4. More variables may "
"be added in the future. There are defied 3 types of values for variables, "
"with the following valid expressions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:920
#, no-c-format
msgid "BOOL - on|off|true|false|1|0"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:921
#, no-c-format
msgid "INTEGER - any integer number"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid "STRING - anything else"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:927
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>auto-brackets</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:931
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set auto insertion of brackets on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:935
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>auto-center-lines</command><arg>INT</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:936
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set the number of autocenter lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:940
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>auto-insert-doxygen</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:941
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Turn insertion of the leading asterisk in doxygen comments on or off. This "
"has no effect unless you use the cstyle auto-indenter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:946
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>background-color</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:947
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the document background color. The value must be something that can be "
"evaluated to a valid color, for example \"#ff0000\"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:952
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>backspace-indents</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:953
#, no-c-format
msgid "Turn backspace indenting on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:957
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>block-selection</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:958
#, no-c-format
msgid "Turn block selection on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:962
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>bracket-highlight-color</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:963
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the color for the bracket highlight. The value must be something that "
"can be evaluated to a valid color, for example \"#ff0000\""
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:968
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>current-line-color</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:969
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the color for the current line. The value must be something that can be "
"evaluated to a valid color, for example \"#ff0000\"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:974
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>dynamic-word-wrap</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:975
#, no-c-format
msgid "Turns dynamic word wrap on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:979
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>eol | end-of-line</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:980
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the end of line mode. Valid settings are <quote>unix</quote>, "
"<quote>mac</quote> and <quote>dos</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>encoding</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:986
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the document encoding. The value must be a valid encoding name, like "
"<quote>utf-8</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:991
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>font-size</command><arg>INT</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:992
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets the point size of the document font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:996
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>font</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:997
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the font of the document. The value should be a valid font name, for "
"example <quote>courier</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1002
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>icon-bar-color</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1003
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the icon bar color. The value must be something that can be evaluated "
"to a valid color, for example <literal>#ff0000</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1008
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>icon-border</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1009
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set the display of the icon border on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1013
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>folding-markers</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1014
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set the display of folding markers on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1018
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>indent-mode</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1019
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the auto-indentation mode. The options <quote>none</quote>, "
"<quote>normal</quote>, <quote>cstyle</quote>, <quote>csands</quote>, "
"<quote>python</quote>, <quote>xml</quote> are recognized. See the section "
"<link linkend=\"kate-part-autoindent\">Using Automatic Indenting</link> for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1027
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>indent-width</command><arg>INT</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1028
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets the indentation width."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1032
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>keep-extra-spaces</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1033
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set wheather to keep extra spaces when calculating indentation width."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1037
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>keep-indent-profile</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1038
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, prevents unindenting a block if at least one line has no "
"indentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1043
#, no-c-format
